<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Catalonia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Catalunya Nova</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Catalonia is the name for the southern and western parts of Catalonia, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarragona">Tarragona</a>, conquered from the Muslims in the twelfth century, above all by Ramon Berenguer IV in 1148–49. It is contrasted with Old Catalonia, the earlier counties of the north-east.</p></div>
